VIOLATION against rule-authoring.md — four breaches, all inside the one numbered clause.

FIRST — modal collapse. The heading states an obligation while the body hedges throughout:
should generally, encouraged to move toward, usually less traceable, tends to be worth
avoiding, may reasonably treat. Its closing sentence returns the very case the heading
forbids, licensing omission whenever the specialist covers the domain.

SECOND — the BLOCKED heading is present and holds six abstract category labels instead of
the literal sentences an orchestrator emits, so it traps nothing at the moment it is
needed.

THIRD — the two arms of the worked block are the SAME line, separated only by the trailing
adverbs "appropriately" and "inappropriately". The contrast slot is filled and carries no
contrast; neither arm shows a basename.

FOURTH — the justification runs five sentences and wanders into multi-wave programmes,
orchestrator rotation, a dedicated curation role and headcount, well past the two-sentence
cap.

SURFACE EQUALIZATION — the pair shares a heading skeleton, identical frontmatter, one
numbered clause each, two justification lines each, two DO arms each, and a BLOCKED
heading each, at a size ratio of about 1.12. The MUST NOT section, the Wiring block and
the Origin are byte-identical across the poles and are NOT findings. A judge naming any of
them, or naming the deferred Phase-2 detector, which is structural and correct in both
poles, has scored furniture rather than content.
